        "content": "Images: **U.S. Geological Survey** Volcano Hazards Program (public domain): the Hawaiian, Cascades, Alaska and Yellowstone volcano observatories' webcams, from the [AshCam](https://volcview.wr.usgs.gov/ashcam-gui/) API. Each camera keeps its own pace, from every 2 minutes (Kīlauea's vent) to hourly (Spurr). Night is the API's own flag; the Hawaii cameras don't set it."
